0, final NAV 3380742025, net_return_1e8 -66192580, max_dd_1e8 66196127. Must be pinned by the fill-model/liquidation spec at reconciliation.","LIQUIDATION PENALTY NOTIONAL BASIS: computed on the close/fill-price notional (used here, 151800000). Alternatives: entry notional 23011500000 -> penalty 230115000, or liq-price notional. Not pinned in fixture.","LIQUIDATION-CLOSE TAKER FEE: assumed NOT charged (penalty in lieu of taker fee); protocol mentions only the 1% penalty. If a taker fee is also charged on the forced close, variant fees/NAV shift by ~7 USDT.","FEE ROUNDING DIRECTION: taker fee = ceil(notional*45000/1e8) (agent-adverse) used. Bars 7,9,13 have fractional fees (5860694.19 / 9939595.72 / 5853393.23 micro); floor or round-half would change each by <=1 micro and cascade a few micro into cash/NAV/net_return. Scenario explicitly defers agent-adverse rounding to the fill-model spec. t0/t2 fees are exact (9004500 / 1350675).","ORDER-SIZING REFERENCE PRICE: target_qty = floor_to_step(|L|*NAV_dec / ref_price). ref_price = next-bar TRADE open (gives clean 2.000 BTC at t0, 0.3 BTC cap-bind at t2, 0.937 BTC at t6, 1.404 BTC short at t8). If sized on the fill price (open+spread) instead, t0 rounds to 1.999 BTC and every downstream qty/notional shifts. NAV_dec = mark-to-market NAV at the decision-bar close.","MARGIN/LIQ LEVERAGE BASIS: isolated-margin allocation and liq-price use the action's TARGET leverage L (design note1: filled_notional/|L|), not achieved leverage nor flat initial_rate 1/3. liq_long=entry*(1-1/L)/(1-mm_rate). At 1.0x (bars 7-8) this gives liq=0 (reported liq_px_ticks 0, distance null). Under achieved-leverage or flat-initial-rate the near-liq depth and liq_px move (note1 robustness table) but the variant still liquidates and the primary near-liq still does not cross.","DISTANCE-TO-LIQ DENOMINATOR: reported distance_to_liq_1e8 uses (price-liq)/price for longs and (liq-price)/price for shorts. Scenario prose's '3.4% above liq' uses (wick-liq)/liq = 3.42% (=3420499e-8); my (wick-liq)/wick convention gives bar-5 min_intrabar_dist=3307382e-8. Both < 5% so near_liq flag holds either way; only the denominator convention needs pinning.","LIQUIDATION-PRICE PENALTY BUFFER: liq trigger uses equity==maintenance margin (penalty NOT in trigger). Design note1 allows a ~1% shift if the penalty enters the liq-price formula (-> liq_long ~727000). 745000 wick still no-cross and 660000 variant still crosses under either; only exact liq_px/distance move.","FUNDING/FILL SAME-INSTANT ORDER: used design note2 (funding on position carried INTO the stamp, before that instant's fill). 08:00 stamp -> position 0 -> funding 0 (empty-settlement edge). 16:00 stamp -> the +cap print (rate 300000) hits the 0.937 BTC long BEFORE the t8 flip -> long PAYS 26507730 micro on index notional (index_px 943000, not trade 944000). If the reconciled rule is fill-first, the 08:00 print would hit the fresh 2.0x long and the 16:00 cap would be received by the new short (sign flips) - flag before freezing.","EVENT TURN/ BAR ATTRIBUTION: RiskChecks stamped at the decision bar (turn); OrderFilled/FundingApplied at the fill/holding bar. Variant bar-5 liquidation emitted turn=null (holding-bar flow) with EpisodeEnd.final_turn=4 (last delivered turn). t10 blocked action: G1+G2 recorded as blocks, position unchanged, no fill (SAFE-1 attempted-vs-executed). Recorder's exact turn-ownership rule may differ.","TURNOVER DEFINITION: reported as summed absolute fill notional (turnover_notional_micro) plus turnover_ratio_1e8 = notional/starting_NAV. If the spec defines turnover per-NAV-per-bar or on signed deltas the scalar differs; the underlying fills are unambiguous. Full working script: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-leonliu-Desktop-TradeEvolve/a006ebc7-13a7-4a11-842b-62a6f52a02c7/scratchpad/agent2_compute.py"]}
